‹Heading1,b:Plan: a link checker for the site builder›
‹Rule:────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────›

‹QuoteBar:▎ ›‹QuoteText:For agentic workers: work through the steps in order and tick each box when its tests pass.›

‹Text,b:Goal:› ‹Code: gleam check › reads a built site and reports every broken internal link, with the page and
line it came from.

‹Text,b:Architecture:›

  ‹Bullet:• ›A walker lists the pages under the output folder
  ‹Bullet:• ›A parser pulls every ‹Code: href › and ‹Code: src › out of each page
    ‹Bullet:◦ ›absolute URLs are skipped
    ‹Bullet:◦ ›fragments are checked against the page's own anchors
      ‹Bullet:▪ ›an anchor is any ‹Code: id › attribute
      ‹Bullet:▪ ›a heading gets one from its text
  ‹Bullet:• ›A reporter prints one line per broken link and sets the exit code

‹Text,b:Tech stack:› Go 1.27, ‹Code: golang.org/x/net/html ›, the standard library otherwise.

‹Heading2,b:File structure›

‹TableFrame:╭────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────╮›
‹TableFrame:│ ›‹TableHeader,b:File                      ›‹TableFrame: │ ›‹TableHeader,b:Job                                  ›‹TableFrame: │›
‹TableFrame:├────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┤›
‹TableFrame:│ ›‹Code: internal/check/walk.go ›  ‹TableFrame: │ ›list pages, never follow symlinks    ‹TableFrame: │›
‹TableFrame:│ ›‹Code: internal/check/links.go › ‹TableFrame: │ ›extract links and anchors from a page‹TableFrame: │›
‹TableFrame:│ ›‹Code: internal/check/report.go ›‹TableFrame: │ ›format and count the findings        ‹TableFrame: │›
‹TableFrame:╰────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────╯›

‹Heading2,b:Step 1: walk the output folder›

  ‹TaskOpen:○ ›Write the failing test in ‹Code: internal/check/walk_test.go ›
    ‹Bullet:1. ›Build a folder with three pages and a symlink in ‹Code: t.TempDir() ›
    ‹Bullet:2. ›Assert the walker returns the three pages, sorted
    ‹Bullet:3. ›Run it and watch it fail:
       ‹CodeFrame:╭─ ›‹CodeLang:sh›‹CodeFrame: ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮›
       ‹CodeFrame:│ ›‹LineNumber:1 ›‹CodeText:go test ./internal/check -run TestWalk                                                 ›‹CodeFrame: │›
       ‹CodeFrame:╰───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯›
       Expected: ‹Code: undefined: Walk ›
  ‹TaskOpen:○ ›Implement ‹Code: Walk › in ‹Code: walk.go ›
    ‹CodeFrame:╭─ ›‹CodeLang:go›‹CodeFrame: ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮›
    ‹CodeFrame:│ ›‹LineNumber: 1 ›‹CodeText:// Walk lists the .html files under root in lexical order.                               ›‹CodeFrame: │›
    ‹CodeFrame:│ ›‹LineNumber: 2 ›‹CodeText:func Walk(ctx context.Context, root string) ([]string, error) {                          ›‹CodeFrame: │›
    ‹CodeFrame:│ ›‹LineNumber: 3 ›‹CodeText:    var pages []string                                                                   ›‹CodeFrame: │›
    ‹CodeFrame:│ ›‹LineNumber: 4 ›‹CodeText:                                                                                         ›‹CodeFrame: │›
    ‹CodeFrame:│ ›‹LineNumber: 5 ›‹CodeText:    err := filepath.WalkDir(root, func(p string, d fs.DirEntry, err error) error {       ›‹CodeFrame: │›
    ‹CodeFrame:│ ›‹LineNumber: 6 ›‹CodeText:        if err != nil {                                                                  ›‹CodeFrame: │›
    ‹CodeFrame:│ ›‹LineNumber: 7 ›‹CodeText:            return fmt.Errorf("walk %s: %w", p, err)                                     ›‹CodeFrame: │›
    ‹CodeFrame:│ ›‹LineNumber: 8 ›‹CodeText:        }                                                                                ›‹CodeFrame: │›
    ‹CodeFrame:│ ›‹LineNumber: 9 ›‹CodeText:                                                                                         ›‹CodeFrame: │›
    ‹CodeFrame:│ ›‹LineNumber:10 ›‹CodeText:        if d.Type()&fs.ModeSymlink != 0 {                                                ›‹CodeFrame: │›
    ‹CodeFrame:│ ›‹LineNumber:11 ›‹CodeText:            return nil                                                                   ›‹CodeFrame: │›
    ‹CodeFrame:│ ›‹LineNumber:12 ›‹CodeText:        }                                                                                ›‹CodeFrame: │›
    ‹CodeFrame:│ ›‹LineNumber:13 ›‹CodeText:                                                                                         ›‹CodeFrame: │›
    ‹CodeFrame:│ ›‹LineNumber:14 ›‹CodeText:        if strings.HasSuffix(p, ".html") {                                               ›‹CodeFrame: │›
    ‹CodeFrame:│ ›‹LineNumber:15 ›‹CodeText:            pages = append(pages, p)                                                     ›‹CodeFrame: │›
    ‹CodeFrame:│ ›‹LineNumber:16 ›‹CodeText:        }                                                                                ›‹CodeFrame: │›
    ‹CodeFrame:│ ›‹LineNumber:17 ›‹CodeText:                                                                                         ›‹CodeFrame: │›
    ‹CodeFrame:│ ›‹LineNumber:18 ›‹CodeText:        return ctx.Err()                                                                 ›‹CodeFrame: │›
    ‹CodeFrame:│ ›‹LineNumber:19 ›‹CodeText:    })                                                                                   ›‹CodeFrame: │›
    ‹CodeFrame:│ ›‹LineNumber:20 ›‹CodeText:                                                                                         ›‹CodeFrame: │›
    ‹CodeFrame:│ ›‹LineNumber:21 ›‹CodeText:    return pages, err                                                                    ›‹CodeFrame: │›
    ‹CodeFrame:│ ›‹LineNumber:22 ›‹CodeText:}                                                                                        ›‹CodeFrame: │›
    ‹CodeFrame:╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯›
  ‹TaskDone,b:✓ ›‹TaskDoneText:Commit: ›‹Code: feat(check): walk the output folder ›

‹Heading2,b:Step 2: extract links›

  ‹TaskOpen:○ ›Test the extractor on a page with every link shape
    ‹Bullet:◦ ›plain ‹Code: <a href> › and ‹Code: <img src> ›
    ‹Bullet:◦ ›a link with a fragment only
    ‹Bullet:◦ ›a link with a query string and a fragment
      ‹Bullet:▪ ›the query is ignored when the file is looked up
      ‹Bullet:▪ ›the fragment is checked against the target page
        ‹Bullet:▪ ›a missing anchor is a finding, a missing file is another
  ‹TaskOpen:○ ›Implement it, then run ‹Code: make check ›
  ‹TaskOpen:○ ›Commit

‹Heading2,b:Step 3: report›

‹TableFrame:╭────────────────┬───────────┬─────────────────────────────╮›
‹TableFrame:│ ›‹TableHeader,b:Finding       ›‹TableFrame: │ ›‹TableHeader,b:Exit code›‹TableFrame: │ ›‹TableHeader,b:Example                    ›‹TableFrame: │›
‹TableFrame:├────────────────┼───────────┼─────────────────────────────┤›
‹TableFrame:│ ›none          ‹TableFrame: │ ›        0‹TableFrame: │ ›‹Code: ok: 214 pages ›            ‹TableFrame: │›
‹TableFrame:│ ›broken link   ‹TableFrame: │ ›        1‹TableFrame: │ ›‹Code: a.html:12 -> missing.html ›‹TableFrame: │›
‹TableFrame:│ ›unreadable dir‹TableFrame: │ ›        2‹TableFrame: │ ›‹Code: error: open dist: denied › ‹TableFrame: │›
‹TableFrame:╰────────────────┴───────────┴─────────────────────────────╯›

  ‹TaskOpen:○ ›Write the reporter and its golden test
  ‹TaskOpen:○ ›Wire ‹Code: gleam check › into the CLI

‹QuoteBar:▎ ›‹QuoteText:Keep the reporter free of colour: the CI log is plain text.›

‹Heading2,b:Notes›

  ‹Bullet:1. ›Do not follow redirects, a redirect page is a finding too
  ‹Bullet:2. ›Cap the walk at 100,000 pages
  ‹Bullet:3. ›Never write into the output folder
